  "response": "Here's a Python function called `bank_rollback(balance, transactions)` that applies transactions in order and returns the final result:\n\n```python\ndef bank_rollback(balance, transactions):\n    \"\"\"\n    Apply transactions to the account balance in order.\n    If balance becomes negative at any point during processing, \n    return (original_balance, False).\n    \n    Args:\n        balance (int/float): Initial account balance\n        transactions (list of int/float): List of transaction amounts\n    \n    Returns:\n        tuple: (final_balance or original_balance, success_flag)\n               - If all transactions succeed without balance going negative:\n                 (final_balance, True)\n               - If balance becomes negative during processing:\n                 (original_balance, False)\n    \"\"\"\n    current_balance = balance\n    \n    for transaction in transactions:\n        current_balance += transaction\n        if current_balance < 0:\n            return (balance, False)\n    \n    return (current_balance, True)\n```\n\n### Example Usage:\n```python\n# Example from requirements\nresult = bank_rollback(100, [50, -30, -200])\nprint(result)  # Output: (100, False)\n\n# All transactions successful\nresult = bank_rollback(100, [50, -30, -60])\nprint(result)  # Output: (60, True)\n\n# Empty transactions list\nresult = bank_rollback(100, [])\nprint(result)  # Output: (100, True)\n\n# Balance becomes negative on first transaction\nresult = bank_rollback(50, [-30])\nprint(result)  # Output: (50, False)\n\n# Negative initial balance\nresult = bank_rollback(-50, [100])\nprint(result)  # Output: (-50, False)\n```\n\n### Key Features:\n- Returns `(original_balance, False)` if balance ever becomes negative during transaction processing.\n- Returns `(final_balance, True)` only if all transactions are completed without balance going below zero.\n- Handles edge cases such as empty transaction lists and already-negative starting balances.",
